    "q-92799": {
      "dom_id": "step-q92799",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Dominick has $8$ steel marbles and $14$ glass marbles. What number is missing from the boxes in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of steel marbles to glass marbles is $4:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $4$ steel marbles for every $\\boxed{}\\,$ glass marbles.",
      "worked_solution": "Since there are $8$ steel marbles and $14$ glass marbles, the ratio of steel marbles to glass marbles is $8:14.$\n\nWe can simplify this ratio by dividing both numbers by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\,8 &  & : & \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,14 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,↓÷\\,\\,2 &  \\\\ \\,\\,\\,4 &  & : &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,7 & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThat means that $4:7$ is equivalent to $8:14.$ \n\nSo, the complete statement is\n\"The ratio of steel marbles to glass marbles is $4:7$ because there are $4$ steel marbles for every $7$ glass marbles.\"\n\nHence, the missing number is $7.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
